+### 0825 — M0-bound macOS and deterministic harness runtime factories (TASK-260715-3ejhyy)
+- IMPLEMENTATION: The macOS production call site validates the exact accepted manifest SHA-256 and semantic evidence before any component closure runs, derives the accepted packet/HEV/SSH values from that manifest, and creates one fresh coordinator graph per generation. The graph selects `LibSSH2TransportFactory`, the system-domain Keychain resolver, mandatory approved-host-policy and privacy-safe mapper inputs, injected TCP/DNS and network-settings seams, and a bridge-backed M1 packet plane. The deterministic SPM harness implements the same candidate-neutral `TunnelRuntimeFactory` without a production-manifest bypass.
+- OWNERSHIP: Packet-plane `prepare` constructs only Swift owners. The first descriptor, readiness source, private listener, HEV lease/thread, and PacketFlow read remain inside `PacketFlowBridge.start`, reached only by the separate post-settings `activateReads` call. Stop is idempotent; existing coordinator and bridge owners retain reverse cleanup ordering.
+- NEGATIVE EVIDENCE: Runtime tests reject digest narrowing before every component factory, disabled permission, supersession, selected libssh2 pin drift, and a missing mandatory PacketBridge capability. Dispatch tests admit ordinary TCP CONNECT, route virtual-DNS TCP/UDP to DNS, and reject all other UDP as deferred.
+- VERIFICATION: The focused composition and harness suites pass 9/9; the full SwiftPM run passes 503 tests in 42 suites with the existing 25 known unavailable-ReluxNIOSSH issues. Strict Swift format, Core boundary guard, 32 M0 binding negatives, accepted manifest/repository validation, native/libssh2 pin inspection, three SPM target builds, and unsigned macOS Debug/Release host/provider generation, target tests, linkage, and graph validation all exit 0. The first focused compile and first lint run exited 1 on test-double types and mechanical formatting, then passed after correction. The first provider gate exited 2 before generation because the task worktree's two-line Tuist pin was untrusted; after explicitly trusting that exact `mise.toml`, pinned Tuist 4.202.5 validation passed.
