/Users/iv/.codex/skills/project-management/README.md:305:- `agent_context` is presentation-only: it never weakens board, lifecycle, provider, model, or review gates. It defaults to `{"profile":"full"}`. Local mode reads root `agent_context`; remote mode reads `remote.agent_context`, falling back to root when absent or `null`. `profile` accepts `full|lite`; nested `prompt`, `queries`, and `responses` values are strict enums. Bare `project_config()` always returns the role-optional general config, while an explicit `project_config(view=spawn-preflight, role=ROLE, agent=PROVIDER?)` or role-targeted call returns the narrow preflight projection and requires a valid role. Full prompts retain the full role template and body except for a legacy Markdown `Definition of Done` section: role baseline DoD is rendered once from frontmatter, merged with the task checklist. `lite` is explicit opt-in via `agent_context.profile = "lite"` or `--context-profile lite`; it selects a compact role contract that retains concrete FIRST/LAST commands, merged DoD, task-scoped outcome evidence, reviewer verdict branches, Stop-The-Line, task inputs, and workdir while removing the generic CLI/reporting narrative. Its default `prompt.preconditions` policy is `{"mode":"budgeted","inline_bytes":2048}`: text smaller than `inline_bytes` remains inline, while larger text (and binary resources) is materialized read-only under `.temp/resources/` and represented by name, description, byte count, SHA-256 digest, and path. Set `mode:"inline"` to retain normal text inlining; the full profile defaults to that behavior. A lite text `spawn` response emits only the run handle, resolved selection (or requested-to-resolved delta), run status, cursor, and one relative `task-board spawn observe ... --until terminal --format compact` command; it omits paths and audit echoes. Full text, `--json`, and the run manifest retain their existing full audit and path evidence. `schema(operation=NAME)` / `schema(mutation=NAME)` provide on-error discovery without a proactive full-schema read. Project overrides are profile-specific: `.agents/spawn-template.md` for full and `.agents/spawn-template-lite.md` for lite. Use `--context-profile full|lite` to force one complete profile for a command.
