+# TASK-260715-3ejhyy — developer outcome
+
+## Result
+
+Ready for review. The macOS production root and deterministic SPM harness root now build the same candidate-neutral `TunnelRuntimeFactory` session graph. Production validates the sole accepted M0 manifest before constructing any runtime dependency. `prepare` only creates the packet-plane session; `activateReads` is the sole `PacketFlowBridge.start` call and therefore remains post-settings.
+
+## Accepted binding pin
+
+- Source: `/Users/iv/Developer/relux-tunnel/.temp/resources/TASK-260715-3ejhyy/TASK-260720-1qhxqa_m0-production-bindings-v1.json`
+- Size: `17492` bytes
+- SHA-256: `40333862b46b7af04cdd966ade91e8c9cc917e573c6601e26e7fa956d11ae161`
+- Schema/task/revision semantics, `productionCompositionPermitted`, supersession state, upstream evidence digests, selected HEV/libssh2/bridge pins, compatibility rows, and mandatory capabilities are all fail-closed gates at the production call site `MacOSProductionDependencyFactory.makeRuntime()`.
+- Missing and unreadable sources have distinct errors; digest drift is rejected before decoding; semantic negatives cover disabled permission, supersession, pin drift, and missing mandatory capability. No component closure is invoked on rejection.
+
+## Implemented scope
+
+- Added candidate-neutral M1 packet-plane preparation/session/dispatch types in `ReluxTunnelCore`.
+- Added macOS production binding validation and one-graph-per-generation composition in `ReluxTunnelMacOSAdapter`.
+- Selected the existing libssh2 transport, accepted PacketFlow/HEV path, immutable configuration, mandatory host policy, system-domain Keychain credentials, privacy-safe diagnostics, clocks, metrics, logging, cancellation, memory pressure, settings seams, TCP and DNS consumers through existing boundaries.
+- Added deterministic harness session factory with the same root interface and generation semantics, without a production-manifest bypass.
+- Enforced TCP CONNECT, virtual-DNS TCP/UDP dispatch, and explicit rejection of all other M1 UDP.
+- Existing coordinator and bridge ownership contracts retain reverse-order release and idempotent repeated stop.
+- iOS, route/tuning selection, TCP/DNS internals, reconnect, general UDP, and provider implementation changes remain excluded as required.
+
+## Verification
+
+| Gate | Result | Evidence |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Focused composition + harness tests | exit 0, 10/10 | `swift-test-composition-04.log`, `swift-test-harness-factory-02.log` |
+| Full SwiftPM suite (final code) | exit 0, 504 tests / 42 suites, 25 known unavailable-ReluxNIOSSH issues | `swift-test-full-03.log` |
+| Core / macOS adapter / harness target builds | exit 0 | `swift-build-core-01.log`, `swift-build-macos-adapter-01.log`, `swift-build-harness-support-01.log` |
+| Final unsigned macOS provider Debug build | exit 0, arm64+x86_64 | `xcodebuild-provider-debug-final.log` |
+| Full macOS host/provider Debug+Release validation | exit 0 | `macos-targets-validate-02.log` |
+| Core boundary guard | exit 0 | `check-core-boundaries-01.log` |
+| M0 manifest validation | exit 0 | `m0-bindings-check-01.log` |
+| M0 negative suite | exit 0, 32 tests | `m0-bindings-test-01.log` |
+| Native/libssh2 pin and linkage checks | exit 0 | `check-native-dependencies-01.log` |
+| Strict Swift format (final) | exit 0 | `swift-format-lint-05.log` |
+| `git diff --check` | exit 0 | `git-diff-check-final.log` |
+
+All logs are under `.temp/TASK-260715-3ejhyy/` in the story worktree.
+
+## Preserved failures and anomalies
+
+- The first focused test compile exited 1 for test-double type mistakes and passed after correction (`swift-test-composition-01.log`).
+- The first strict lint exited 1 for mechanical formatting and passed after formatting (`swift-format-lint-01.log`).
+- The first provider matrix exited 2 because the exact two-line `mise.toml` was locally untrusted. After `mise trust ./mise.toml`, pinned Tuist 4.202.5 validation passed (`macos-targets-validate-01.log`, `mise-trust.log`, `macos-targets-validate-02.log`).
+- The first final full SwiftPM run exited 1 when the pre-existing libssh2 pressure fixture returned `.cancelled` instead of `.resourceLimitExceeded` under full-suite concurrency. Its exact isolated rerun passed 1/1 and the immediate full rerun passed 504/504. Both failure and recovery evidence are retained (`swift-test-full-02.log`, `swift-test-channel-pressure-rerun-01.log`, `swift-test-full-03.log`).
+- `task-board validate` exits 0 but reports the parent story is still `to-dev` while this child is `development`; that parent aggregate status is orchestrator-owned (`task-board-validate.log`).
+- Pre-existing M0 manifest/docs/script worktree changes were preserved and not incorporated into this task's implementation scope.
+
+## Review focus
+
+Review `MacOSProductionDependencyFactory.makeRuntime()` for fail-before-construction ordering, `BridgeBackedM1PacketPlaneFactory.prepare()` for pure preflight, and `BridgeBackedM1PacketPlaneSession.activateReads()` for the only accepted bridge start. Negative tests name and exercise these bounds.
